  "prompt": "## plate\nTASK:\nRedraw the attached image EXACTLY, with one change: remove the middle third lantern, middle second lantern, middle left lantern, middle right lantern, top second lantern, top left lantern. Paint what is behind them.\n\nThe attached image is hono chochin.\n\nRULES:\n- Keep everything else exactly the same: shape, size, position, colours, shading and camera. Do not move, resize, rotate or redraw anything else.\n- Where the removed things were, paint what was behind them. Continue the art around them in the same style: a door, a wall, a trunk, a beam. Nothing new may appear.\n- Keep the solid flat background #FF00FF.\n- No text, no labels, no characters, no extra props.\n\nSTYLE:\nSTYLE LOCK: Cozy cat mobile game in the style of Meow Tower (Hyperbeard).\n\nPRIMARY GOAL: Warm, cheerful, cute sprites for a phone game with a flat top-down map where every object stands up and faces the camera. Everything must look like one illustrator painted it with flat colour blocks and a soft brush, with no pen lines.\n\nCORE AESTHETIC: Lineless, softly shaded colour blocks. Chunky, pillowy, slightly bulging shapes with big rounded corners, like soft toys or cushions. Warm, sunny, cheerful colour: soft but saturated, never neon, never muted or grey. Cats are white with a few small grey or orange patches, a wide head, small rounded ears set wide, tiny dark dot eyes set wide apart, a tiny mouth, no outline, no tail.\n\nEDGES: NO OUTLINES. No dark contour line around any shape. Shapes are separated by colour alone. Where a shape meets a similar colour, it has a slightly darker band of its own hue along its lower or outer edge (a wall with a darker apricot base band, a roof with a darker red lip, a window with a darker wood frame). Edges are soft and very slightly brushy, not hard vector edges. Inner detail is a darker same-hue shape, never a dark line. The only dark colour is tiny facial features.\n\nCOLOR: Warm cheerful palette measured from Meow Tower. Main